-- title:
--   Lemma 3.1: the A-HPE inequalities (3.3)–(3.6)
-- statement:
--   Let $f:\mathbb R^n\to\mathbb R$ be convex and differentiable, $h$ proper closed convex, $F=f+h$, and let $\{x_k,y_k,\tilde x_k,\tilde y_k\}$ be generated by Algorithm 1 (the A-HPE framework) with parameter $0<\sigma<1$, through iteration $k\ge1$. Let $x_*$ be the projection of $x_0$ onto the set $X_*$ of minimizers of $F$, $F_*=F(x_*)$ the optimal value, and $D=\operatorname{dist}(x_0,X_*)$. Then $F(y_k)<+\infty$ and
--
--   1. $\displaystyle \frac12\|x_*-x_k\|^2+A_k\big(F(y_k)-F_*\big)+\frac{1-\sigma^2}2\sum_{j=1}^k\frac{A_j}{\lambda_j}\|\tilde y_j-\tilde x_{j-1}\|^2\le\frac12D^2;$ (3.3)
--   2. $\displaystyle \sum_{j=1}^k\frac{A_j}{\lambda_j}\|\tilde y_j-\tilde x_{j-1}\|^2\le\frac{D^2}{1-\sigma^2};$ (3.4)
--   3. $\displaystyle A_k\ge\frac14\Big(\sum_{j=1}^k\sqrt{\lambda_j}\Big)^2;$ (3.5)
--   4. if $y_j=\tilde y_j$ for $j=1,\dots,k$, then $\displaystyle\|y_k-x_*\|\le\Big(\frac2{\sqrt{1-\sigma^2}}+1\Big)D.$ (3.6)
--
--   These are the estimates of Monteiro and Svaiter (Theorems 3.6, 3.10 and Lemma 3.7 of their paper) that the analysis of the optimal tensor method builds on: (3.3) bounds the optimality gap by $D^2/(2A_k)$, and (3.4)–(3.5) control the growth of $A_k$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $F$ takes values in `EReal`; the inequality (3.3) is stated for the finite reals $F(y_k)$ and $F(x_*)$. The projection is given as a minimizer $x_*$ with $\|x_0-x_*\|=D$.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - generalization: sequence generated by Algorithm 1, whose STEP 2 stops when 0 ∈ ∂F(y_k) → runs that satisfy STEPS 1, 3, 4 at every iteration, whether or not 0 ∈ ∂F(y_j); reason: every run of the printed algorithm is such a run; the estimates do not use the stopping test
--   - encoding: (3.3) with F(y_k) − F_* real → conjunct F(y_k) ≠ ⊤ and (3.3) with toReal of F(y_k) and F(x_*); reason: F is EReal-valued; F(y_k) is finite in every run, so the real form is the printed one
--   - encoding: x_* the projection of x₀ onto X_*, D the distance → x_* ∈ X_* with dist(x₀, x_*) = infDist(x₀, X_*) = D; reason: this characterizes the projection; X_* is closed and convex
--   - encoding: (3.6) when y_k is chosen as ỹ_k for all k → hypothesis y_j = ỹ_j for 1 ≤ j ≤ k; reason: a run through k has no iterations after k
--   - encoding: h : ℝⁿ → (−∞, +∞] proper closed convex, F = f + h → h : E → EReal never ⊥, somewhere finite, lower semicontinuous, with convex epigraph; F x = (f x : EReal) + h x; reason: Lean convention for extended-valued convex functions; same instances
--   - encoding: ε_{k+1} a scalar ε ≥ 0 (∂_ε is defined for ε ≥ 0, p.6) → ε_{k+1} ∈ ℝ with no sign condition in the Algorithm 1 run; reason: for proper F, (3.1) at y = ỹ_{k+1} forces ε_{k+1} ≥ 0 (and ∂_εF is empty where F = +∞), so the runs are the same
-- source:
--   Jiang, Wang & Zhang, An Optimal High-Order Tensor Method for Convex Optimization, arXiv:1812.06557v3, Lemma 3.1, pp.7–8 (Algorithm 1, p.7)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_TensorAHPE_Problem
import Definitions.Def_TensorAHPE_AHPE

open Finset

namespace TensorAHPE

/-- **Lemma 3.1 (the A-HPE inequalities (3.3)–(3.6)).**
Jiang, Wang & Zhang, arXiv:1812.06557v3, Lemma 3.1, pp.7–8: "Suppose the sequence
{x_k, y_k, x̃_k, ỹ_k} is genernated from Algorithm 1. Let x_* be the projection of x₀ onto the set
of optimal value points X_*, F_* be the optimal value, and D be the distance from x₀ to X_*. Then
for any integer k ≥ 1, it holds that (Theorem 3.6 in [24]),
(1/2)‖x_* − x_k‖² + A_k(F(y_k) − F_*) + ((1 − σ²)/2) Σ_{j=1}^{k} (A_j/λ_j)‖ỹ_j − x̃_{j−1}‖² ≤ (1/2)D². (3.3)
Therefore, Σ_{j=1}^{k} (A_j/λ_j)‖ỹ_j − x̃_{j−1}‖² ≤ D²/(1 − σ²). (3.4)
Furthermore, A_k and λ_k has the following relation (Lemma 3.7 in [24])
A_k ≥ (1/4)(Σ_{j=1}^{k} √λ_j)². (3.5)
If y_k is chosen as ỹ_k for all k, the distance between y_k and x_* can be bounded as follows
(Theorem 3.10 in [24]), ‖y_k − x_*‖ ≤ (2/√(1 − σ²) + 1) D. (3.6)"

Setting: problem (1.1), p.2, with `f` differentiable and convex and `h` proper closed convex;
`F = f + h`; a run of Algorithm 1 (p.7) with parameter `σ` through iteration `k ≥ 1`; `x_*` a
minimizer of `F` at distance `D = dist(x₀, X_*)` from `x₀` (the projection).

**Formalization Note.** `F` is `EReal`-valued; the first conjunct `F(y_k) ≠ +∞` makes the real
form of (3.3) meaningful (`F(y_k)` and `F_* = F(x_*)` are then finite reals, read with `toReal`).
The run omits Algorithm 1's STEP 2 (see `IsAlg1Run`). In (3.6) "y_k chosen as ỹ_k for all k" is
assumed for the iterations `1, …, k` of the run. -/
theorem lemma_3_1 {n : ℕ} (f : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → ℝ) (h : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → EReal)
    (hf : ConvexOn ℝ Set.univ f) (hfd : Differentiable ℝ f) (hh : IsProperClosedConvex h)
    (σ : ℝ) (s : Alg1Seq n) (k : ℕ) (hk : 1 ≤ k) (hrun : IsAlg1Run (compositeObj f h) σ s k)
    (xstar : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) (hxstar : xstar ∈ minSet (compositeObj f h))
    (hproj : dist (s.x 0) xstar = Metric.infDist (s.x 0) (minSet (compositeObj f h))) :
    compositeObj f h (s.y k) ≠ ⊤ ∧
    1 / 2 * ‖xstar - s.x k‖ ^ 2
        + s.A k * ((compositeObj f h (s.y k)).toReal - (compositeObj f h xstar).toReal)
        + (1 - σ ^ 2) / 2 * ∑ j ∈ Icc 1 k, s.A j / s.lam j * ‖s.yt j - s.xt (j - 1)‖ ^ 2
      ≤ 1 / 2 * Metric.infDist (s.x 0) (minSet (compositeObj f h)) ^ 2 ∧
    ∑ j ∈ Icc 1 k, s.A j / s.lam j * ‖s.yt j - s.xt (j - 1)‖ ^ 2
      ≤ Metric.infDist (s.x 0) (minSet (compositeObj f h)) ^ 2 / (1 - σ ^ 2) ∧
    1 / 4 * (∑ j ∈ Icc 1 k, Real.sqrt (s.lam j)) ^ 2 ≤ s.A k ∧
    ((∀ j, 1 ≤ j → j ≤ k → s.y j = s.yt j) →
      ‖s.y k - xstar‖
        ≤ (2 / Real.sqrt (1 - σ ^ 2) + 1) * Metric.infDist (s.x 0) (minSet (compositeObj f h))) := by sorry

end TensorAHPE
